# Normalize line endings for this cross-platform project. Git stores
# everything as LF internally regardless of the values below; "text=auto"
# only controls what's checked OUT into your working directory.
#
# We force LF on checkout for all source files too (even on Windows), so
# the repo stays consistent for Linux/Jetson builds and diffs don't get
# polluted by line-ending-only changes. MSVC, VS Code, and Visual Studio
# all handle LF-only C++ files without issue.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.cpp text eol=lf
*.h text eol=lf
*.hpp text eol=lf
*.cmake text eol=lf
CMakeLists.txt text eol=lf
*.qrc text eol=lf
*.qss text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.gitignore text eol=lf
*.gitattributes text eol=lf

# Windows-native files that genuinely want CRLF
*.sln text eol=crlf
*.vcxproj text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Binaries -- never touch these
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.zip binary
*.exe binary
*.dll binary
